The problem seems to be occurring when a package contains a `script` integration twice.

e.g.,

```yaml
script: !include scripts.yaml
script manual: !include_dir_merge_named scripts
```

from the example given above. I can confirm this is broken (0.114.dev0).

I've been debugging a little bit, and currently think this goes south in the dict merge:

https://github.com/home-assistant/core/blob/72b0f957195b572409e2c677256beb60da26f9d3/homeassistant/config.py#L632-L633

Added in 2 debugging lines to the above function to see what is happening:

```py
    _LOGGER.error(f"Recursive merge current conf {json.dumps(conf, indent=2)}")
    _LOGGER.error(f"Recursive merge for {json.dumps(package, indent=2)}")
```

